    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0734" n="692" xml:id="pg692"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 14, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 12th instant, soliciting a delay in the sale of the
                    prize vessel Peterhoff and its cargo until appeal can be had to the Supreme
                    Court, and to state that the matter has been referred to the Secretary of the
                    Navy.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, your lordship’s obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons.</hi></p>
                    <p>Another note was addressed to Lord Lyons, of the same date and in the same
                        words as the above, relative to the Springbok.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
